    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1615">

                <pb facs="1016" n="900" xml:id="pg900"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/76.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Letcher.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-05-05T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 5, 1914, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secretary of Labor states that newspaper reports of intention to modify
                    regulations for admission of Chinese without foundation, but that “Whenever it
                    becomes necessary in the interest of humanity and to save the lives of refugees
                    to give them temporary asylum that course is being followed.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
